---
const paths = [
 {name:'Embedded',route:['Application + SQLite library','Local database and journal','Other connections on this host'],steps:[
  ['Application + SQLite library','The application calls the library in its own process. There is no database network hop. A second application process on the same host may open another connection to the same file.'],
  ['Local database and journal','The connection claims writer access and changes the local database through its journal or WAL. One writer at a time means a long transaction can hold up other writers.'],
  ['Other connections on this host','Other local writers must wait or fail according to the actual busy-handling contract. Adding web workers does not add independent write capacity to this file.'],
  ['Local database and journal','A successful commit has the durability of the selected settings and storage. Losing the host and its only volume requires a recovery copy elsewhere.']
 ]},
 {name:'Server',route:['Application → connection pool','Network → PostgreSQL primary','Optional standby on another host'],steps:[
  ['Application → connection pool','The request first needs a connection. A pool bounds server sessions, but an exhausted pool adds waiting before any SQL runs. Include that wait in the request deadline.'],
  ['Network → PostgreSQL primary','The primary executes the transaction, checks constraints and coordinates conflicting writers. The application can run on several hosts without each owning the data files.'],
  ['Optional standby on another host','Replication adds another copy. An asynchronous standby may lack the latest commit; a synchronous commit can wait for its configured standby acknowledgement and add latency.'],
  ['Network → PostgreSQL primary','The reply travels back over the connection. A missing reply leaves the client uncertain even if the commit is safe. A standby becomes useful only with a tested promotion and reconnection path.']
 ]},
 {name:'Distributed',route:['Application → SQL gateway','Transaction data on several machines','Required replica acknowledgements'],steps:[
  ['Application → SQL gateway','The client connects to a SQL gateway. Connecting nearby does not establish that the rows or the transaction work are nearby. Their placement must be checked separately.'],
  ['Transaction data on several machines','A transaction touching several data ranges may send work to several machines. A shared inventory row can remain a contention point even as the cluster grows.'],
  ['Required replica acknowledgements','The system coordinates the replicas required by its contract. Surviving a failure requires enough appropriately placed replicas to remain reachable; extra distance can enter the commit path.'],
  ['Application → SQL gateway','The result returns through the gateway. Failed coordination may require transaction retry, while an uncertain reply still requires reconciliation. More nodes do not eliminate the application contract.']
 ]}
];
---
<figure class="selection-boundary" data-selection-boundary data-paths={JSON.stringify(paths)}>
 <figcaption><span>Figure 1</span> Follow one reservation across the boundary</figcaption>
 <p class="note">Illustrative paths, not measurements. Compare the same step in each arrangement.</p>
 <div class="choices" role="group" aria-label="Database arrangement">{paths.map((p,i)=><button type="button" data-path={i} aria-pressed={i===0}>{p.name}</button>)}</div>
 <ol class="route" aria-label="Where this reservation travels">{paths[0].route.map((label,i)=><li data-place={i} class:list={[i===0&&'current']}><span>{i+1}</span><strong>{label}</strong></li>)}</ol>
 <div class="explanation" aria-live="polite"><p data-stage>{paths[0].steps[0][0]}</p><p data-story>{paths[0].steps[0][1]}</p></div>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Boundary playback"><button type="button" data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><output data-position>Step 1 of 4</output></div>
 <details><summary>Read all three paths</summary>{paths.map(p=><div><p><strong>{p.name}</strong></p><ol>{p.steps.map(s=><li>{s[0]}: {s[1]}</li>)}</ol></div>)}</details>
</figure>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-selection-boundary]').forEach(root=>{
  const paths=JSON.parse(root.dataset.paths!); let variant=0, step=0, timer:ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>|undefined;
  const el=(s:string)=>root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(s)!;
  const stop=()=>{clearTimeout(timer);timer=undefined;el('[data-play]').textContent='Play';};
  const render=()=>{
   const path=paths[variant], current=path.steps[step];
   el('[data-stage]').textContent=current[0];el('[data-story]').textContent=current[1];
   root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-place]').forEach((place,i)=>{place.querySelector('strong')!.textContent=path.route[i];place.classList.toggle('current',path.route[i]===current[0]);});
   root.querySelectorAll('[data-path]').forEach((b,i)=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(i===variant)));
   el('[data-back]').setAttribute('aria-disabled',String(step===0));el('[data-next]').setAttribute('aria-disabled',String(step===3));
   el('[data-position]').textContent=`Step ${step+1} of 4`;
  };
  root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-path]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{stop();variant=Number(b.dataset.path);render();}));
  el('[data-back]').addEventListener('click',()=>{stop();step=Math.max(0,step-1);render();});
  el('[data-next]').addEventListener('click',()=>{stop();step=Math.min(3,step+1);render();});
  el('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click',()=>{stop();step=0;render();});
  const tick=()=>{render();if(step===3){stop();return;}el('[data-play]').textContent='Pause';const words=paths[variant].steps[step].join(' ').split(/\s+/).length;timer=setTimeout(()=>{step++;tick();},Math.max(8000,words*60000/170+3000));};
  el('[data-play]').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(timer){stop();return;}if(step===3)step=0;tick();});
  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{if(document.hidden)stop();});render();
 });
</script>
<style>
 .selection-boundary{border:1px solid var(--color-rule);background:var(--color-surface);padding:1rem;margin:2rem 0}figcaption{font-weight:650}figcaption span{display:block;font-size:.75rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);text-transform:uppercase}.note{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.choices,.controls{display:flex;gap:.45rem;flex-wrap:wrap}button{font:inherit;font-size:.85rem;min-height:44px;padding:.5rem .7rem;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface-alt);border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:.25rem;cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{box-shadow:inset 0 -3px var(--color-text)}button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.5}button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-text);outline-offset:3px}.route{padding:0;list-style:none;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.6rem}.route li{padding:.65rem;border:1px dashed var(--color-rule);font-size:.85rem;min-width:0}.route span{display:block;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.route .current{border:2px solid var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface-alt)}.explanation{min-height:11rem;border-left:3px solid var(--color-text);padding:.1rem .8rem;margin-bottom:1rem}.explanation p:first-child{font-size:.85rem;font-weight:650}.explanation p:last-child{font-size:.95rem}.controls output{font-size:.8rem;align-self:center}details{font-size:.85rem;margin-top:1rem}summary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px}@media(max-width:540px){.route{grid-template-columns:1fr}.route li{display:flex;gap:.6rem}.selection-boundary{padding:.75rem}.explanation{min-height:13rem}.controls button{flex:1}.controls output{flex-basis:100%}}
</style>
